@flexiarg apparatus/supply-the-misattribution-hypothesis
@title Supply the Misattribution Hypothesis With the Failure Report
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 3 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-cejaj6 turn-cfViZm turn-siorRn; first proposed for: A routing tool has misdelivered a message for the second time, after a fix was ordered.
@why [futon-theory/rapid-debugging]

! conclusion: Attach the intended-vs-actual pair and the operator's causal hypothesis to the failure report, as diagnostic input rather than verdict.

  + IF:
    The operator can observe both the intended and the actual routing and has a hypothesis about the mechanism (voxterm 'thought it was for you').

  + HOWEVER:
    A bare recurrence report leaves the agent to rediscover what the operator already saw; over-asserting the hypothesis could mislead the diagnosis.

  + THEN:
    Attach the intended-vs-actual pair and the operator's causal hypothesis to the failure report, as diagnostic input rather than verdict.

  + BECAUSE:
    Rapid debugging (I4: any bug diagnosable in under 10 minutes) depends on context arriving with the report; this specialises it: the operator hands over the routing pair and mechanism hypothesis so the diagnosis starts minutes ahead.
